      },
      {
       "content": "{% set z = [('Living room','living_room'),('Bedroom','bedroom'),('Kids room 1','kid1'),('Kids room 2','kid2')] %}{% set ns = namespace(l=[]) %}{% for n, k in z %}{% set h = state_attr('input_datetime.climate_rad_hold_' ~ k, 'timestamp') | float(0) %}{% if h > now().timestamp() + 1800 %}{% set ns.l = ns.l + ['**' ~ n ~ '** set by hand until ' ~ (h | timestamp_custom('%H:%M'))] %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{{ ns.l | join('  \\n') if ns.l else 'Every radiator follows its room target.' }}\n\n<details><summary><ha-icon icon=\"mdi:information-outline\"></ha-icon></summary>\n\nWith **Radiators follow room targets** on, each radiator valve is set from its room's day or night target; off, the Tado schedules run. A radiator changed by hand keeps its setting until the time shown.\n\n**AC boosts when behind by**: the room's AC helps only once the room is this far below target. **Morning warm-up lead**: how many minutes before the night ends the warm-up starts.\n\n</details>",
       "type": "markdown",
       "visibility": [
        {
         "condition": "state",
         "entity": "automation.climate_radiators",
         "state": "on"
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "heading": "House mode",
       "heading_style": "subtitle",
       "icon": "mdi:home-thermometer-outline",
       "type": "heading"
      },
      {
       "content": "<details><summary><ha-icon icon=\"mdi:information-outline\"></ha-icon></summary>\n\nThe outdoor temperature picks the house mode: below **Heat below** the house heats, above **Cool above** it cools, in between nothing runs. *Heat below* must stay under *Cool above*, or all comfort control stands down. To leave a season the outdoor temperature has to pass the threshold by the house hysteresis (under Safety).\n\n</details>",
       "text_only": true,
       "type": "markdown"
      },
      {
       "cards": [
        {
         "color": "deep-orange",
         "entity": "input_number.climate_heat_below_outdoor",
         "features": [
          {
           "style": "buttons",
           "type": "numeric-input"
          }
         ],
         "grid_options": {
          "columns": 6
         },
         "name": "Heat below",
         "type": "tile"
        },
        {
         "color": "light-blue",
         "entity": "input_number.climate_cool_above_outdoor",
         "features": [
          {
           "style": "buttons",
           "type": "numeric-input"
          }
         ],
         "grid_options": {
          "columns": 6
         },
         "name": "Cool above",
         "type": "tile"
        }
       ],
       "columns": 2,
       "square": false,
       "type": "grid"
      },
      {
       "heading": "Day / night",
       "heading_style": "subtitle",
       "icon": "mdi:weather-night",
       "type": "heading"
      },
      {
       "content": "<details><summary><ha-icon icon=\"mdi:information-outline\"></ha-icon></summary>\n\nNight targets apply while the alarm is armed for the night. The night schedule only moves the alarm at its edges, 21:00 and 06:00; arming or disarming by hand wins.\n\n</details>",
       "text_only": true,
       "type": "markdown"
      },
